From a57cad6077e8e8c88746b366219d161894097fbf Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Khaled <khaledchoucri@gmail.com>
Date: Sun, 4 Oct 2026 21:55:07 +0300
Subject: [PATCH] POC-7: catching, trainer battles, EXP/level-up/move
 learning/evolution after grid battles

- Poke Balls from the Custom screen (an item slot used instead of chips): Emerald's
  Cmd_handleballthrow odds (catch rate, ball bonus, HP, sleep/freeze x2, poison/burn/paralysis
  x1.5, Net/Dive/Nest/Repeat/Timer/Master), shake animation, Pokedex flags, nickname
  (DoNamingScreen), GiveMonToPlayer / PC.
- Single trainer battles on the grid: party from CreateNPCTrainerParty (exported), trainers send out
  their next Pokemon, no running / catching, Teleport fails, trainer EXP x1.5, prize money
  (GetTrainerMoneyToGive, Amulet Coin), victory music by class, white-out on a loss.
  Double-battle trainers, Frontier, Hill, secret bases stay vanilla.
- EXP per fainted opponent as Cmd_getexp (sent-in split, Exp. Share, Lucky Egg, traded, EVs),
  given level by level after the battle with Emerald's MonTryLearningNewMove and the
  delete-a-move flow through the real summary screen (HM moves protected), then
  GetEvolutionTargetSpecies -> EvolutionScene after a win. Pay Day money. Pokerus on exit.
- Self-test hooks: PKBN_TEST_BALLS / _THROW / _TRAINER / _EVOLVE / _FORGET, PKBN_AUTO_PRESS.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01FbWSqvcg6G5Gpw6ynvR5tJ
